In the previous discussion, James sought guidance on how to load and save GeoTIFF files using `libtiff`, transitioning from an outdated `tiffIO` package. I provided sample code for reading a GeoTIFF file into a 2D vector, ensuring dimensions matched expected values. For saving, I shared a method to write data organized in a single vector to a GeoTIFF file, emphasizing the need to set appropriate TIFF tags. Next, he inquired about updating a function to determine data types, shifting from `typeid` checks to a more modern `if constexpr` approach using `std::is_same`. I suggested simplifying by mapping directly to `libtiff`'s types without a custom enum, thereby streamlining integration with TIFF operations.
